vow 'count' is 'Int' in version 1 and 'Float' in version 2; supply it with vow count = expr
vow 'fresh' is new in version 2 and has no default; supply it with vow fresh = expr
rename 'url' -> 'address': the vow is 'String' in version 1 and 'Int' in version 2; set 'address' with vow address = expr, reading prior.url
retire names the vow 'legacy'; a vow version 2 lacks is dropped with no item
prior.items is 'List<Int>' in version 1, a type version 2 no longer declares
version 1 has no vow 'missing' to read through prior
amends vow 'note' is set twice
prior is the instance of the amended version, not a value; read one of its vows as prior.NAME
rename names 'ghost', which version 1 never had
amends vow 'span' is both set and the target of rename 'stamp' -> 'span'; a name takes one item
